window.bookSummaryJSON = "‘Devoured this captivating romance in one evening without coming up for air… Addictive.’ Reader review⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ <p> <strong>Fake dating never tasted so sweet</strong> </p> <p>When Alice ‘Murph’ Murphy’s mother passed, she vowed to keep the family bakery running – even if it meant letting go of her high school sweetheart, Nash Harris. But when Nash walks back into Piece O’ Cake with a wedding invitation, Murph panics.</p> <p>Desperate to remind him of what they had, she ropes her charming bar-owner friend, Harley Shaw, into a fake relationship.</p> <p>The plan? Make Nash jealous and win him back. But as Murph and Harley spend more time together, their pretend romance starts feeling very real. Now, Murph must decide: chase the past with Nash, or take a chance on the one who never left?</p> Readers LOVE <em>Where We Belong</em>! <p>‘<em>My Best Friend’s Wedding</em> but better! <strong>I was sucked in from the first chapter</strong>. I <strong>laughed, cried and held my breath</strong> a lot.’ ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐</p> <p>‘Emotional depth, drama, <strong>romance, comedy, and witty banter</strong>… A <strong>delightfully entertaining</strong> debut romantic tale that romance fans will certainly enjoy!’ ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐</p> <p>‘A <strong>hilarious, heartfelt</strong> story… A <strong>perfect beach, feel-good read</strong>.’⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐</p> <p>‘<strong>Loved this book</strong>… So enjoyable.’ ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐</p> <p>‘<strong>Moved me to laughter and tears.</strong>’ ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐</p>"; 
